<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Trimmer roots for the WASM client (Rule 1.2).

  Blazor reaches components, layouts and their [Parameter] setters by reflection: the router
  activates a page from a Type, LayoutView instantiates a layout from typeof(MainLayout), and the
  renderer assigns parameters by name. None of that is a static call the trimmer can follow, which
  is exactly what produced the historical 'CtorNotLocated' failure for MainLayout when trimming was
  first attempted (see AGENT.MD).

  Rooting these two assemblies whole is deliberate rather than lazy. They are the small part of the
  output — the size that matters is the framework and Radzen.Blazor, which stay fully trimmed —
  and a per-type root list would have to be edited every time a page or component is added, with
  the failure mode being a runtime error in the browser rather than a build break.

  Shared is rooted for the same reason at one remove: its DTOs are reached through generated JSON
  metadata, and its strongly-typed IDs carry JsonConverter attributes instantiated by the
  serializer.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="PoRepoLineTracker.Client" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="PoRepoLineTracker.Shared" preserve="all" />
</linker>
